{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "24", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "27", "S": "40"}}, "news": [{"title": "Local bodies in Tamil Nadu get expanded powers to approve building plans", "para": "The Tamil Nadu government has simplified the approval process for residential building plans by local bodies. Corporations and municipalities can now approve plans with greater floor space and more dwelling units. Town panchayats and rural bodies have also seen an increase in their approval limits. The height limit for residential and commercial buildings has been increased to enhance the availability of space.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/local-bodies-in-tamil-nadu-get-expanded-powers-to-approve-building-plans/135161146?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-266546/135161146.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "ED raids 13 places across Delhi-NCR, Bengaluru, Chandigarh in fraudulent NRI housing loan case", "para": "The Enforcement Directorate conducted searches at 13 properties associated with a major money laundering case. Focused on fraudulent housing loans secured with forged documents for Non-Resident Indians, the investigation involves entities such as Antriksh Promoters and Developers Pvt Ltd and Sunshine Infrawell Pvt Ltd. The collection of evidence aims to uncover financial irregularities, potentially leading to the seizure of crucial documents and digital assets.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/ed-raids-13-places-across-delhi-ncr-bengaluru-chandigarh-in-fraudulent-nri-housing-loan-case/135161025?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-279666/135161025.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Uttar Pradesh housing board's NOC not needed for building plan approval", "para": "The housing department has announced that property owners will no longer require no-objection certificates from the UP Housing Board. This change abolishes outdated regulations from a 2010 directive, allowing direct submission of building plans to the Lucknow Development Authority. Additionally, betterment fees for housing board schemes will not be included with development authority project fees, streamlining the approval process to foster urban growth in the state.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/uttar-pradesh-housing-boards-noc-not-needed-for-building-plan-approval/135160691?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-264030/135160691.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}